# Audit attribution safety net: if a previous commit's post-commit never fired
# (hooks skipped, crash, or an earlier --no-verify), its staged entries are
# still in .xp-gate/audit.pending.jsonl. Flush them now, stamped with the commit
# they actually belong to (`git log -1`), so they land under a real commit
# instead of accumulating or being stamped with THIS run's hash later. Runs
# before any gate so the flush is never counted in this commit's timings.
# Best-effort and silent: audit must never affect the commit's outcome.
